---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout02.astro";
import Header from "../../../components/02/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../../components/02/Footer.astro";
import Pager from "../../../components/02/Pager.astro";
import Style from "../../../components/02/Style.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="Plate | Variable Target Yaw Control" lang="en">
  <Style />
  <Header current="platef" lang="en"/>

  <main class="part02-main">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h2 class="page-title">Plate</h2>
      <p class="page-lead">
        The control performance and thruster outputs were evaluated for target yaw angles of 0°, ±45°, and ±90°.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Target Yaw 0°</h2>

      <div class="result-layout">
        <div class="result-image result-image-position">
          <img
            src={`${base}/images/02/plate/plate_0_position.png`}
            alt="Initial plate orientation at Target Yaw 0 degrees"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="result-content">
          <h3>Control Result</h3>
          <p>
            The initial orientation of 0° was maintained stably until the end of the simulation.
          </p>

          <img
            class="result-chart"
            src={`${base}/images/02/plate/plate_0.png`}
            alt="Plate control result at Target Yaw 0 degrees"
            loading="lazy"
          />

          <h3>Thruster Output</h3>
          <p>
            Small corrective inputs were continuously applied while maintaining the orientation, with the thrusters operating more frequently than for the other payloads.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Target Yaw +45° / +90°</h2>

      <div class="comparison-grid">
        <article class="result-card">
          <h3>Target Yaw +45°</h3>

          <h4>Control Result</h4>
          <p>
            The payload converged smoothly to the target yaw angle of 45° and maintained a stable orientation afterward.
          </p>

          <img
            class="result-chart"
            src={`${base}/images/02/plate/plate_p45.png`}
            alt="Plate control result at Target Yaw plus 45 degrees"
            loading="lazy"
          />

          <h4>Thruster Output</h4>
          <p>
            Thrust was concentrated during the initial rotation, followed by only small corrective inputs after reaching the target angle.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="result-card">
          <h3>Target Yaw +90°</h3>

          <h4>Control Result</h4>
          <p>
            The payload converged stably to the target yaw angle of 90° and maintained the orientation after reaching it.
          </p>

          <img
            class="result-chart"
            src={`${base}/images/02/plate/plate_p90.png`}
            alt="Plate control result at Target Yaw plus 90 degrees"
            loading="lazy"
          />

          <h4>Thruster Output</h4>
          <p>
            Slightly higher initial thrust was used than in the 45° case, but the output dropped to nearly zero after reaching the target angle.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Target Yaw -45° / -90°</h2>

      <div class="comparison-grid">
        <article class="result-card">
          <h3>Target Yaw -45°</h3>

          <h4>Control Result</h4>
          <p>
            The payload converged smoothly to the target yaw angle of -45° and maintained a stable orientation afterward.
          </p>

          <img
            class="result-chart"
            src={`${base}/images/02/plate/plate_m45.png`}
            alt="Plate control result at Target Yaw minus 45 degrees"
            loading="lazy"
          />

          <h4>Thruster Output</h4>
          <p>
            The output characteristics were symmetric to the +45° case, with the thrusters for the opposite rotation direction used selectively.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="result-card">
          <h3>Target Yaw -90°</h3>

          <h4>Control Result</h4>
          <p>
            The payload converged stably to the target yaw angle of -90° and maintained the orientation after reaching it.
          </p>

          <img
            class="result-chart"
            src={`${base}/images/02/plate/plate_m90.png`}
            alt="Plate control result at Target Yaw minus 90 degrees"
            loading="lazy"
          />

          <h4>Thruster Output</h4>
          <p>
            The output characteristics were symmetric to the +90° case, with only small corrective inputs after the initial rotation.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Control Videos</h2>

      <p>
        The control results for Target Yaw ±45° and ±90° are compared using overall and top views.
      </p>

      <div class="video-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Overall View</h3>
          <video controls playsinline preload="metadata">
            <source
              src={`${base}/videos/02/plate_targets.mp4`}
              type="video/mp4"
            />
          </video>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Top View</h3>
          <video controls playsinline preload="metadata">
            <source
              src={`${base}/videos/02/plate_targets_Cam.mp4`}
              type="video/mp4"
            />
          </video>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Comparison with Part 1</h2>

      <p>
        The Target Yaw +90° control result is compared with the
        <a href={`${base}en/control_model#plate`}>Part 1</a>
        result.
      </p>

      <div class="comparison-grid comparison-grid-wide">
        <article class="result-card">
          <h3>Part 1: Target Yaw +90°</h3>
          <img
            class="result-chart"
            src={`${base}/images/02/plate/plate_old_p90.png`}
            alt="Part 1 plate control at Target Yaw plus 90 degrees"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </article>

        <article class="result-card">
          <h3>Part 2: Target Yaw +90°</h3>
          <img
            class="result-chart"
            src={`${base}/images/02/plate/plate_p90.png`}
            alt="Part 2 plate control at Target Yaw plus 90 degrees"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="comparison-conclusion">
        In Part 1, the payload reached the target angle quickly, but overshoot and continuous thruster output were observed.
        In Part 2, reaching the target takes longer, but the thruster output decreases smoothly as the payload approaches the target angle,
        and the orientation is maintained with almost no thrust after reaching it.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Pager
    prev={{
      title: "H-Steel",
      href: "/en/02/hsteel",
    }}
    next={{
      title: "Truss",
      href: "/en/02/truss",
    }}
  />

  <Footer lang="en" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .result-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(280px, 0.75fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr);
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .result-image img,
  .result-chart {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .result-content h3,
  .result-card h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .result-content p,
  .result-card p {
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .comparison-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .result-card {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .result-card h4 {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.6rem;
  }

  .comparison-conclusion {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 2.5rem auto 0;
    line-height: 1.9;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .video-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .video-grid video {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .video-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>